These two files need to be located in the same directory.
ie: c:\mIRC\scripts
once that is completed, /load -rs c:\path\to\files\wraith.mrc

Currently the script supports mIRC 5.80 and up.
mIRC 7.46+ required for SHA256 (default). mIRC 6.03+ supports MD5 fallback.

type /helpauth once it is loaded.

Setup:
  /setauth <password> <secpass> <authkey> [hashalgo] [botnick]

  hashalgo: sha256 (default) or md5 (for old bots)
  botnick:  optional, for per-bot settings

Examples:
  /setauth mypass mysecpass myauthkey                  (global, sha256)
  /setauth mypass mysecpass myauthkey md5               (global, md5)
  /setauth mypass mysecpass myauthkey sha256 hubot      (per-bot)

Show settings:
  /showauth             (global)
  /showauth hubot       (per-bot)

Manual hash:
  /auth -Auth <challenge> <botnick>

The script auto-responds to -Auth in both DCC chat and private messages.
SHA256 (64 hex chars) is preferred; the bot still accepts MD5 (32 hex chars).

